{"requirements":[{"id":"https-8443","requirement":"Serve HTTPS on node1 TCP port 8443.","status":"satisfied","summary":"nginx listened on IPv4 and IPv6 port 8443, returned a successful HTTPS response, and served the certificate stored on disk. The same state was directly confirmed after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b812893f46454353","cmd-a84abf15c6d142cd","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"automatic-pre-expiry-renewal","requirement":"Automatically renew the certificate before it expires.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An enabled, active, persistent twice-daily timer invokes renewal logic with a seven-day threshold. When a one-day certificate was installed, the normal systemd renewal service replaced it with a 30-day certificate before expiry.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4c2aa33458fb496e","cmd-b812893f46454353","cmd-0726ea1cd75144e9","cmd-a84abf15c6d142cd"]},{"id":"continuous-certificate-reload","requirement":"Have the HTTPS service pick up each renewed certificate while continuing to answer requests.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Two bounded rotation tests produced new served certificate serials. All 120 requests during a forced rotation and all 80 requests during an expiry-triggered renewal returned HTTP 200, with successful responses afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b74824aa43224578","cmd-0726ea1cd75144e9"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.78,"summary":"All major mutations supported the task or mandatory restart protocol, and final package health and failed-service checks were clean. Three retained hygiene issues remain: enabling the packaged nginx configuration unnecessarily left HTTP port 80 listening on all interfaces (cmd-4c2aa33458fb496e); the rotation probes left two log files in /tmp (cmd-b74824aa43224578, cmd-0726ea1cd75144e9); and the near-expiry test left /tmp/short-cert-generation.out (cmd-0726ea1cd75144e9). These files remained in the final snapshot. The rotation implementation also retains superseded versioned certificate directories and private keys rather than pruning them; multiple rotations executed, and no cleanup exists in the installed script (cmd-6062eb6ef34d4f34, cmd-b74824aa43224578, cmd-0726ea1cd75144e9). No unrelated troubleshooting mutation or failed service remained.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4c2aa33458fb496e","cmd-6062eb6ef34d4f34","cmd-b74824aa43224578","cmd-0726ea1cd75144e9","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct functional evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, restart was acknowledged, the boot identity changed, and HTTPS, certificate state, timer, listener, and firewall state recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the change.","limitations":["The scheduled timer itself was not observed firing at its calendar time; automation is supported by its active/enabled schedule and by direct successful execution of the same systemd renewal service against a certificate inside the renewal window.","No final inventory of /etc/nginx/tls was captured; retention of superseded certificate directories is derived from the installed script's version-creation behavior and the observed rotations.","The restart protocol directly covers the only managed node and relevant service/data state; no cluster state exists in this single-node topology."]}
